.TH ZERODDS-NAMING-SVC 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-naming-svc \- standalone OMG CosNaming 1.3 NameService daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-naming-svc
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH=VALUE\fR]...
[\fB\-\-check\-config\fR]
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-persist\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-naming-svc
implements OMG Naming Service 1.3
.RI ( formal/2004-10-03 )
in full:
.BR NamingContext " (bind, rebind, bind_context, rebind_context, resolve,"
.BR unbind ", " new_context ", " bind_new_context ", " destroy ", " list ),
.BR NamingContextExt " (" to_string ", " to_name ", " to_url ", " resolve_str ")"
and
.BR BindingIterator " (" next_one ", " next_n ", " destroy ),
over IIOP and, with a certificate, SSLIOP.
.PP
The root context's object key is
.IR NameService ,
reachable as
.IR corbaloc::host:2809/NameService
(the default port); every other bound context and every live
.B BindingIterator
gets its own object key, so a resolved sub-context or a
.B list
reply's iterator is a fully addressable object in its own right, not a
handle only the root understands.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-persist\-file ,
the whole naming graph is written to that file (atomically: a sibling
temporary file, then a rename) after every operation that changes it, and
read back at start, so a restart keeps its bindings. Without it the graph
is in memory only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Base file, plus \fIFILE\fR.d/. Without it:
.I naming-svc.yaml
and
.I naming-svc.d/
in the system directory. See
.BR zerodds-naming-svc.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-set =\fIPATH=VALUE\fR
One value above all files; repeatable. Every option below except
\fB\-\-version\fR/\fB\-\-help\fR is short for \fB\-\-set\fR of its file key.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-config
Check the configuration, print every value with its origin, exit
0 (valid) or 1 (invalid).
.TP
.BR \-\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
IIOP listen address. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:2809 .
.TP
.BR \-\-advertise\-host =\fIHOST\fR
The host named in every IOR this daemon hands out, when
.B \-\-bind
is a wildcard address. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BR \-\-persist\-file =\fIFILE\fR
Where the naming graph is saved. Without it, nothing is persisted.
.TP
.BR \-\-ssliop\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
SSLIOP listen address; enables SSLIOP. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:2810 .
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
SSLIOP server certificate (PEM).
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
SSLIOP server key (PEM).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the daemon: the accept loops close, the graph is
saved one last time when
.B naming.persist_file
is set, then the process exits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZERODDS_NAMING_ADVERTISE_HOST
The host the IORs name when
.B naming.bind
is a wildcard address; the setting
.BR naming.advertise_host ,
above the files, below
.BR \-\-set .
Default
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 normal stop, 1 configuration, 2 bind, 4 TLS.
.SH FILES
.IR /etc/zerodds/naming-svc.yaml ,
the file named by
.BR naming.persist_file .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-naming-svc.yaml (5),
.BR zerodds-corba-bridged (1).
.SH STANDARDS
OMG Naming Service 1.3
.RI ( formal/2004-10-03 ),
CORBA 3.4, GIOP 1.2, SSLIOP, CSIv2.
.SH AUTHORS
ZeroDDS Contributors.
